id: pmc-milestone-status-roles
title: Use configured done status roles for immutable milestone generation
description: Milestone generation previously selected literal closed rows while correction reads honored configured terminal_done roles. PR #291 now shares one SDK-registry-based first-publication ledger across generation and corrections. This item retains the original follow-up and its regression evidence.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: follow-up,milestones,status-roles
created_at: "2026-10-27T04:42:06.623Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T13:54:18.537Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T13:54:17.657Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T18:06:51.000Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Resolve lifecycle meaning through the SDK status registry, preserve immutable release attribution, and add non-git custom-registry regression evidence."
resolution: "Delivered by PR #291 (cda9e95): Preserve published release claims with linked corrections"
expected_result: "Resolve lifecycle meaning through the SDK status registry, preserve immutable release attribution, and add non-git custom-registry regression evidence."
actual_result: "PR #291 merged at 2026-10-28T18:06:51Z as cda9e95; required CI test (22) and test (26) passed on the merged head."
comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-27T07:44:30.725Z",codex-agent,"Addressed with the shared chronological release ledger for PR #291: SDK status normalization and terminal_done registry roles determine publication ownership. CLI and host generation forward the tracker registry and preserve explicit status filters. Adversarial non-git fixtures include a custom done-role status named active_named_done, early active captures, edits and reopening; the owning frozen row remains stable across 500 catalog permutations."
  "2026-10-27T07:54:18.264Z",codex-agent,"Final regression evidence: test/release-ownership.test.ts passes 4 tests with zero failures/skips/cancels, including 500 catalog permutations, SDK status-role classification, actual host/standalone generation and explicit status filters without git. The linked test command passes. Shared generation/correction behavior is documented in docs/tracker-milestones.md and docs/release-corrections.md."
  "2026-10-27T08:01:34.045Z",codex-agent,"Implementation complete with focused and packed evidence linked on pmc-release-corrections and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. Final-head npm/Bun CI evidence is recorded in the PR after completion. Releasing the claim while retaining this item unclosed for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-27T08:44:46.841Z",codex-agent,"Round-2 fix freezes status meaning at capture, rather than applying current registry roles to historical records. Schema-2 doneItemIds are fingerprint-bound; legacy records keep released semantics. Five real-tracker regressions cover status promotion/demotion and alias changes, 500 round-trip/replay sequences, diagnostics, explicit filters, existing correction accessibility and actual host/standalone commands without git. All five pass; related suite 48 passes. Producer, ledger and rendering behavioral revert proofs each fail. The role follow-up is now addressed without permitting future registry edits to change historical publication."
  "2026-10-27T09:06:13.186Z",codex-agent,"Final packed validation in pmc-release-corrections passed all 112 checks across 8 launchers and 6 install modes, preserving both schema-1 and schema-2 correction chains after registry edits. Canonical legacy token compatibility, frozen publication, live roles and selection diagnostics are covered; related suite 48 and final publication file 5 pass. Full npm/Bun CI evidence will be linked with counts in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. Releasing this claim and retaining the item unclosed."
  "2026-10-27T10:58:58.732Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 extends the shared role context through every closure-policy consumer: duplicate/invalid/canceled terminal dispositions, neutral issue wording, grouping, breaking/semver, diagnostics, counters, exports, contracts and upgrade projections. Frozen done-role captures remain terminal after current roles change. 168 focused tests pass, including 500 SDK-registry/alias sequences and actual standalone/host commands without git; closure-policy coverage is 100 percent in all configured dimensions. Four isolated function reverts fail. No concrete non-blocking inline finding was supplied; all identified instances of literal closed semantics in these paths are replaced with SDK/context decisions."
  "2026-10-27T11:33:35.208Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 packed consumer proof passes 168 checks across 6 install modes and 8 real npm/Bun/host/npx/bunx launchers. All 56 added closure-role checks pass after registry role edits: duplicate claims omitted and refused by correction commands, neutral closures remain neutral, semver/diagnostics/counters agree. Related cohort 51 and focused closure cohort 168 pass. Full CI and CodeQL are queued; pending is not approval. Exact run URLs and final evidence remain on pmc-release-corrections and PR #291."
  "2026-10-27T11:48:40.278Z",codex-agent,"Round-3 closure semantics fix, packed consumers and five behavioral revert proofs are complete; both claims are released and items remain unclosed for orchestrator verification. Current-main and final-test head a750079 is pushed. Full npm/Bun Node 22/26 gates remain queued with zero steps at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40498185138; CodeQL remains pending. Counts are pending, not passes. The bounded handoff, exact local evidence, public-copy numbers and SDK observations are recorded on pmc-release-corrections and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291."
  "2026-10-27T15:07:35.133Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 extends frozen-role ownership to actual publication. The shared generator selector now decides ledger claims, so a custom done-role duplicate can be reopened and repaired in a later release without the omitted capture reserving ownership. Frozen omission diagnostics are separate from claims and cannot hide later native rows. A 500-item native SDK lifecycle state machine covers 2-4 releases, done/active/canceled custom roles, all non-change dispositions, query filters, reopenings, repairs, immutable rendered claims and correction chains. Dedicated native empty-title and host/standalone JSON/TOON regressions cover other omitted rows. Disposable CI mutation copies prove both the omitted-capture defect and the round-2 mutable-role defect; fixed source is restored in finally before the model runs again. Focused/packed/real-data evidence and unchanged-threshold exact-head npm/Bun results are maintained in PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291; pending checks are never counted as passes."
  "2026-10-27T15:54:31.280Z",codex-agent,"Round-4 class fix and invariants are recorded; runtime proof remains pending. At 15:52 UTC the focused lifecycle job had zero steps executed at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40532517260, so neither behavioral mutant failure nor the restored model is counted as proven yet. Full npm/Bun gates depend on focused proof and remain pending. Exact-head verification, prior measured baseline and bounded handoff are tracked on pmc-release-corrections and PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/pull/291. Own claims remain released; items remain unclosed for orchestrator verification."
